  "question_user": "how much information does likelihood training on TR0+TS0 carry about each direction class?",
  "registered": "2026-10-12, before any sampling",
  "registered_test_user": "the contrast/null ratio of mean I (8 contrast vs 8 random null directions) exceeds 1: bootstrap 95% CI lower bound > 1. No magnitude predicted. THE ONLY REGISTERED TEST.",
  "report_user": "every I(v) also as the Cramer-Rao standard error 1/sqrt(I(v)) in kcal/mol",
  "reported_check_not_a_prediction_user": "I(v) > 0 for every random null direction (bootstrap lower bound). It cannot fail: a sum of variances is positive for any direction some competing structure uses. Reported beside the exact zero for N1 and N2, because 'Type A exactly 0, Type B above 0' is the taxonomy's central point.",
  "scope_user": "E1 measures likelihood training only. Margin training, which is MXfold2's loss, sees competing structures only through the highest-scoring one, and E1 does not measure it.",
  "spectrum_user": "eigenvalues of N_nt^T F N_nt (426 x 426); split-half noise floor = largest |eigenvalue| of (F_A - F_B)/2, halves = first and second K/2 samples; report how many eigenvalues fall below 1% of the median contrast information, and how many below the noise floor",
  "theory_user": "for P(s|x) proportional to exp(-c(s).theta/kT), the Hessian of -log P(ref|x) is Cov_P[c(s)]/(kT)^2, independent of the reference; I(v) = sum over sequences of Var_{s~P(.|x)}[c(s).v]/(kT)^2 at Turner 2004, d0, special_hp 0, 37 C"
